# Code only. Everything a run produces is reproducible from it and is large.
runs/
*.log

# The four reports are the readable record of why the data looks the way it
# does, and a reader without the 3.7 GB parquet cannot regenerate them. They
# are a few hundred kB each, so they live in the tree.
*.pdf
!RaViLa_report_v1_prepare.pdf
!RaViLa_report_v2_training.pdf
!RaVL-Autobench.pdf
!RaVL_dataset_v2.pdf

# Data and model artefacts never belong in the tree -- paths.py points at them.
*.parquet
*.pt
*.zip
checkpoints/

# The executed copies are committed too. They were treated as a local
# verification artefact, but the outputs are the point for a reader without the
# data: the executed notebook is the only place the frames, the radar scatter
# and the per-task counts are visible without a machine that holds the 3.45 GB
# parquet. All six together are 1.1 MB.

# Local mirror of what was sent to the dashboard.
wandb/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
*.orig
*.swp
